{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Only the firstling that is firstborn to YHWH among beasts—no man may sanctify it.</b> From here we learn that the offerings are not changed, for example an olah offering may not be changed into shelamim, nor shelamim into a sin-offering, and so for all of them. And they said in the Sifre: I have only the firstling; from where do I derive that for all consecrated things one may not change them from one sanctity to another sanctity? Scripture says: 'among beasts—no man may sanctify it' — that is, it derives from itself, for when it says 'among beasts—no man may sanctify it,' it means another sanctity; rather, it stands in its first sanctity."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:04.332451749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}